# Local development overrides for the dashboard (`yarn dev` only).
#
# `vite build` uses mode "production" and therefore reads `.env.production`
# (absent -> nginx defaults apply: base "/"). `yarn build:e2e` uses mode "e2e"
# and reads `.env.e2e`. So this file cannot affect either shipped artifact.
#
# The base stays "/" on purpose.
#
# The router's route table is written as `/dashboard`, `/dashboard/trash`,
# `/dashboard/favorites`, ..., `/board/:id`. Those paths assume the app is
# mounted at the root, which is what production does (nginx serves the dashboard
# at `/` and the editor at `/app/`). Mounting the dashboard under a prefix in
# dev would double-count it - `/dashboard` would have to become
# `/dashboard/dashboard` - so the prefix is not an option without restructuring
# the URLs. See UPSTREAM_SYNC.md's deployment notes and memory/MEMORY.md.

# The editor is proxied at `/editor` on this same origin, which is what keeps
# IndexedDB shared between the two apps in development.
VITE_EDITOR_BASE=/editor
